# 70-story-kernel-tpm.rules — grant the unprivileged story-kernel runtime
# user direct access to the in-TD vTPM devices.
#
# story-kernel.service runs as User=story-kernel with an empty
# CapabilityBoundingSet and opens /dev/tpmrm0 (falling back to /dev/tpm0)
# directly to seal/unseal the DKG key share. The swtpm --vtpm-proxy device
# is created at boot with no owning group, and this hardened image
# deliberately ships no `tss`/`tpm` group, so without this rule the device
# defaults to root:root 0600 and every TPM call fails with EACCES.
#
# /dev/tpm0 is in subsystem "tpm" and /dev/tpmrm0 in subsystem "tpmrm", so we
# match on KERNEL name (not SUBSYSTEM) to cover both. Mode stays 0600: the
# device is owned by the single runtime user, not shared via a group.
KERNEL=="tpm[0-9]*",   OWNER="story-kernel", GROUP="story-kernel", MODE="0600"
KERNEL=="tpmrm[0-9]*", OWNER="story-kernel", GROUP="story-kernel", MODE="0600"
